{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Every male.</b> Even one with a blemish. Why is this stated? If for eating, it is already stated: ״the bread of his God, from the most holy things״ (Leviticus 21) — rather, to include those with blemishes for division (Sifra)." "<b>Whatever touches, etc.</b> Lesser sacred offerings or ordinary offerings that touch it and absorb from it." "<b>Shall become holy.</b> To become like it — if it is disqualified, they are disqualified; and if it is valid, they are eaten according to the law of the meal-offering (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:13.061840061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}